  leftText: 
  rightText: Pit Spiders, while being able to produce webbing, hardly ever do so.
    Instead, they save their energy by residing in abandoned hare dens, awaiting
    to pounce on any prey. This behavior is speculated to be the reasoning why hares
    are so willing to abandon old burrows in favor of making brand new ones.
